WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.800
When the end of “Eternals” hits, it’s
as if someone picked an enormous white dandelion

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.990
and blew on it, scattering its seeds all over
the universe.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.539
If your head is still spinning, you’ve come
to the right place.

00:00:13.539 --> 00:00:15.910
This is the end of "Eternals," explained.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.039
"Eternals assemble."

00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:22.850
Most of “Eternals” is concerned with “the
emergence,” an event triggered by the energy

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:28.550
expelled when half of the world’s population
was snapped back into existence in “Avengers:

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.550
Endgame.”

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.190
This caused a literal earthquake that once
again gave rise to the Deviants — mortal

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:39.100
foes of the Eternals — and began triggering
a series of events that would lead to the

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:44.010
Celestials’ newly-revealed long-game: bringing
an end to human life through the emergence

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:50.000
of Tiamut, a Celestial "egg" planted eons
ago who has been feeding off human evolution

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.160
all this time.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:56.410
To paraphrase one character: all along, the
Eternals have been basically farming humans

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.340
as food for the Celestials.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:04.479
The emergence begins, marked by an exploding
volcano and the sight of Tiamut seemingly

00:01:04.479 --> 00:01:07.329
rising up from the center of the planet.

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:12.250
Just as his hand and part of his head begins
to emerge, he is turned to marble.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.280
At this point, the Eternals are fractured.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:19.799
Ikaris has revealed his cruel intentions (and
that he murdered Ajak), and Sprite has let

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:24.210
puppy love get the better of her, joining
Ikaris in a quest to assist the Celestials

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:26.539
as they bring about the end of mankind.

00:01:26.539 --> 00:01:32.060
Meanwhile, a conflicted Kingo has bailed,
and with another recently deceased, that leaves

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:36.810
Sersi, Phastos, Druig, and Makkari to fight
the good fight.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:43.319
As speculated by Phastos, the remaining Eternals
can unite their power to create what he calls

00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:44.719
“the Uni-Mind.”

00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:50.369
First introduced by Jack Kirby in 1977’s
“Eternals” #12, the Uni-Mind has served

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:54.899
the group over the years as their weapon of
choice against the Celestials, so it’s only

00:01:54.899 --> 00:01:57.070
appropriate that they’d deploy it here.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:02.820
In the comics, Uni-Mind has often been depicted
as a being of light and energy; in the film,

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:07.030
the group emanates yellow tendrils of energy
that link them together.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:12.890
Since at this point, Sersi is the Prime Eternal,
she is the principal beneficiary of the Uni-Mind;

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:15.970
in the comics, typically only the Prime Eternal
can summon it.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:20.610
When Phastos is able to contain Ikaris on
the beach and Druig delivers a crushing blow

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:26.160
to the duplicitous Sprite, it frees up the
remaining Eternals to maximize their Uni-Mind

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.000
potential, stopping the emergence in its tracks
and seemingly saving the day.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:36.370
While a lot of this is going on, Thena finds
herself grappling with The Deviant Warlord

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:41.560
Kro, presented in this film as being essentially
the most powerful Deviant.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:46.090
Of course, she’s also grappling with issues
of mind and memory, as she has been throughout

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:50.070
most of the film — only, now the audience
understands that her memory issues aren’t

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:54.430
so much an inability to remember as an inability
to forget.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:59.680
Kro has a weapon the other Deviants do not
wield — he can speak, which means he can

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.300
manipulate.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.930
Throughout their epic battle, Kro attempts
to confuse and even befriend the Eternal,

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:10.870
and as her eyes glaze over, it looks like
his tactic might be working.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:15.120
By the end of their confrontation, Thena is
wrapped up in Kro’s tendrils, about to have

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.660
her energy drained, much like Ajak before
her.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.380
But our girl has a trick up her sleeve.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:26.111
At seemingly the last moment, Thena activates
the golden spear she wields throughout the

00:03:26.111 --> 00:03:31.320
film — which doesn’t seem to be an object,
so much as it is a manifestation of her cosmic

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:35.090
powers — and slices Kro into several pieces.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:39.680
One of the cool things about this scene is
that, in the comics, Thena and Kro were romantic

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.820
partners for thousands of years.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.940
It was a relationship that was forbidden,
since both the Eternals and Deviants are sworn

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:50.360
enemies — but if you’re aware of such
a storyline, the scene probably played even

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:54.400
better, because you may have thought there
was a chance Kro and Thena could indeed come

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.400
together.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:04:02.900
With the day seemingly saved, and the emergence
seemingly avoided, one group of Eternals return

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:07.200
to the Domo to head off in search of their
next adventure, while another group stays

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.450
behind on Earth.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:12.980
It is this latter group that feeds one of
the film’s cliffhangers.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:17.889
Just as Sersi seems to be reunited with Dane
Whitman and preparing for her happily ever

00:04:17.889 --> 00:04:23.199
after, she is literally snatched off the planet
by a vengeful Arishem — who holds the Earth-bound

00:04:23.199 --> 00:04:28.310
Eternals before him, speaking to them in space
with their planet now relegated to the background

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:29.310
of the shot.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.400
As it turns out — big surprise!

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:35.389
— Arishem isn’t thrilled by how the Eternals
betrayed their supposed duty.

00:04:35.389 --> 00:04:40.360
He also isn’t nearly so easy to defeat in
battle, which is why he now holds the Eternals

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:45.370
before him as if they were misbehaving mice,
promising to return for judgment.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:50.599
As if that statement isn’t ominous enough,
in the comics Arishem is often referred to

00:04:50.599 --> 00:04:55.340
as “Arishem the Judge” and it isn’t
because he has a tendency to let people off

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:57.820
with a slap on the wrist and a stern warning.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:03.469
Typically, he has the ability to judge which
planet’s civilizations will live and die,

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:06.349
and is the most powerful of the Celestial
Hosts.

00:05:06.349 --> 00:05:12.080
The bottom line: when some future MCU movie
presents Arishem’s judgment, it most likely

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.599
will not be good news.

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:20.400
After a few dozen names scroll past, the screen
lights back up to reveal the interior of the

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.020
Domo, where our space-traveling Eternals have
received word that their counterparts on Earth

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:26.870
are being judged by Arishem.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:32.000
It’s just then that a cosmic event occurs,
depositing two space travelers into their

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.000
ship.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.800
Pip, a smart-alecky, small-in-stature CG character
voiced by Patton Oswalt, introduces Harry

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:42.980
Styles as Eros, the royal prince of Titan,
aka Thanos' brother.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:45.630
"I love those guys."

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:48.330
For Marvel fans, all of this is big news.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:53.479
Eros is a very unorthodox character in the
comics, known primarily for his hedonistic

00:05:53.479 --> 00:05:55.680
lifestyle and hard-partying ways.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.020
In the comics, he went on to join the Avengers
— where he earned the new Earthbound name

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:05.510
Starfox — and became as adept at putting
down baddies as he was at bedding women.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:09.599
Although they don’t get into all this is
the post-credits scene, Eros is the son of

00:06:09.599 --> 00:06:14.539
two Eternals himself, has frequently battled
Thanos and has comic book connections to such

00:06:14.539 --> 00:06:18.919
characters as Ultron and the upcoming Disney+
series star “She-Hulk."

00:06:18.919 --> 00:06:24.110
Not to be overshadowed is Pip, who seems to
be serving as a valet for Eros.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:29.309
Pip is a character some fans have been clamoring
for, and there was a substantial groundswell

00:06:29.309 --> 00:06:32.659
not long ago to get Peter Dinklage cast in
the part.

00:06:32.659 --> 00:06:37.760
Eros says to the Eternals as the scene concludes,
“Your friends are in big trouble.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:39.490
And we know how to find them.”

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:46.189
In the second post-credits scene, we see the
pay-off for a tease that Dane Whitman seemed

00:06:46.189 --> 00:06:47.979
to be making at the end of the film.

00:06:47.979 --> 00:06:52.919
As he was reunited with Sersi, who was eager
to reveal all about her world-saving adventure

00:06:52.919 --> 00:06:58.139
and desire to remain on Earth, Harington’s
Dane had his own revelation to make, saying

00:06:58.139 --> 00:07:01.219
that his family history is "complicated."

00:07:01.219 --> 00:07:06.470
That conversation was interrupted — perhaps,
forever — when Arishem rudely interrupted

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:09.289
and swept Sersi away for intergalactic judgment.

00:07:09.289 --> 00:07:13.590
In the second post-credits moment, we see
a conflicted Dane in what looks to be a university

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:18.150
building room or library, examining a strange-looking
box.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:22.860
Inside is a sword (undoubtedly the magical
Ebony Blade), which seems to be activating

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:29.490
itself as Dane says “Death is my reward,”
and “I’m sorry, I have to try.”

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:34.599
Just as something is about to happen, an off-camera
voice indicates that someone substantial has

00:07:34.599 --> 00:07:36.270
entered the room, undetected.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:38.779
“Are you sure you’re ready for that?”

00:07:38.779 --> 00:07:42.590
the voice asks, seemingly interrupting Dane’s
ritual.

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:43.689
What does it mean?

00:07:43.689 --> 00:07:47.729
Well, “Dane Whitman” is the name of an
incarnation of the Black Knight, a Marvel

00:07:47.729 --> 00:07:52.000
character dating back to 1967’s “The Avengers”
#47.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:56.490
In a nutshell, this character inherited a
mystical sword wielded by others who bore

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:00.369
the same moniker, using it for both good and
bad.

00:08:00.369 --> 00:08:05.080
This family history goes all the way back
to the time of King Arthur, and the Dane Whitman

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:10.680
character assists the Avengers frequently,
perhaps most notably against Kang the Conqueror,

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:13.879
supposedly the big bad of this newest Marvel
phase.

00:08:13.879 --> 00:08:18.809
Also, the Ebony Blade has been known to allow
its wielder to travel across various time

00:08:18.809 --> 00:08:23.740
streams, which could be very handy in a fractured
multiverse.

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:28.819
The Ebony Blade was originally supposed to
appear as an Easter egg in 2016’s “Doctor

00:08:28.819 --> 00:08:30.930
Strange,” but was dropped at some point.

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:35.620
We might see the Black Knight sooner than
you’d think, as rumor has it that Harington

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:41.300
will appear in 2022’s “Doctor Strange
in the Multiverse of Madness.”

